<B>Parameters of this class are:</B><BR><BR>
<table class="doxtable" border="1" width="100%" cellpadding="4">
<tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Restrictions</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>filename</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top">fiams</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">The filename to use for naming the output files</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>dir_output</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top"></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">The path to the directory where the output files will be placed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>resolution</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">float</td><td style="vertical-align:top">1.2e05</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">The instrument settings: resolution</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>polarity</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top">positive</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">positive, negative</td><td style="vertical-align:top">The instrument settings: polarity</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>max_mz</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">int</td><td style="vertical-align:top">1500</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">Maximum mz</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>bin_step</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">int</td><td style="vertical-align:top">20</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">The size of the step to recalculated the bin size used for adding up spectra along the time axis</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><i>positive_adducts</i></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top">CHEMISTRY/PositiveAdducts.tsv</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">For the accurate mass search. This file contains the list of potential positive adducts that will be looked for in the database. Edit the list if you wish to exclude/include adducts. By default CHEMISTRY/PositiveAdducts.tsv in OpenMS/share is used! If empty, the default will be used.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><i>negative_adducts</i></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top">CHEMISTRY/NegativeAdducts.tsv</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">For the accurate mass search. This file contains the list of potential negative adducts that will be looked for in the database. Edit the list if you wish to exclude/include adducts. By default CHEMISTRY/NegativeAdducts.tsv in OpenMS/share is used! If empty, the default will be used.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>store_progress</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string</td><td style="vertical-align:top">true</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">true, false</td><td style="vertical-align:top">If the intermediate files should be stored in the output directory</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>db:mapping</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string list</td><td style="vertical-align:top">[CHEMISTRY/HMDBMappingFile.tsv]</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">For the accurate mass search. Database input file(s), containing three tab-separated columns of mass, formula, identifier. If 'mass' is 0, it is re-computed from the molecular sum formula. By default CHEMISTRY/HMDBMappingFile.tsv in OpenMS/share is used! If empty, the default will be used.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>db:struct</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">string list</td><td style="vertical-align:top">[CHEMISTRY/HMDB2StructMapping.tsv]</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">For the accurate mass search. Database input file(s), containing four tab-separated columns of identifier, name, SMILES, INCHI.The identifier should match with mapping file. SMILES and INCHI are reported in the output, but not used otherwise. By default CHEMISTRY/HMDB2StructMapping.tsv in OpenMS/share is used! If empty, the default will be used.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>sgf:frame_length</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">int</td><td style="vertical-align:top">11</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">SavitzkyGolayFilter parameter. The number of subsequent data points used for smoothing</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>sgf:polynomial_order</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">int</td><td style="vertical-align:top">4</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">SavitzkyGolayFilter parameter. Order or the polynomial that is fitted</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="vertical-align:top"><b>sne:window</b></td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">int</td><td style="vertical-align:top">10</td>
  <td style="vertical-align:top">&nbsp;</td><td style="vertical-align:top">SignalToNoiseEstimatorMedianRapid parameter. Signal-to-noise estimation window (in mz)</td>
</tr>
</table>
<br>
<b>Note:</b>
<UL style="margin-top:0px;">
  <LI> If a section name is documented, the documentation is displayed as tooltip.
  <LI> Advanced parameter names are italic.
</UL>
